Project scope
-------------

BeefTV is a local-first, single-user desktop workspace for AI-assisted video
creation. The desktop application uses a React user interface embedded by
Wails and a Go backend that listens on loopback. Projects, canvas state,
generated assets, model-channel settings, and durable task state are stored in
the user's local workspace. Requests leave the device only when a user invokes
an externally configured model provider or another explicitly networked tool.

Upstream source
---------------

This repository contains code derived from the following upstream projects:

  Infinite Canvas
  https://github.com/basketikun/infinite-canvas
  Base version: v0.5.0
  Base commit: 568f0f1838df8de31fe885a4e130e2f346dd14ab

Infinite Canvas, maintained by basketikun, provides the upstream infinite
canvas architecture and portions of the canvas implementation used by BeefTV,
including node dragging and zooming, connections, undo/redo, and canvas
import/export. The project was relicensed to MIT in commit
890ba95858bbb13496d23978003716656109abb2. Its copyright and permission notice
are preserved in Part B of LICENSE.

  影策 Open AI Canvas (ddcat-ai/open-ai-canvas)
  https://github.com/ddcat-ai/open-ai-canvas
  Base version: v1.3.0 (2026-09-15)
  Base commit: b7484c56789a7cf1ea7c062084d56af5c3dd18cd

BeefTV is developed on top of ddcat's Open AI Canvas, an AI filmmaking and
short drama workspace. Foundational capabilities derived from this project
include canvas node workflows, model provider integration, task and asset
management, and community-contributed built-in plugins, which BeefTV adapts and
extends for its local desktop application. The referenced release uses the MIT
License; its upstream copyright notices for basketikun and for ddcat and Open AI
Canvas contributors are set out in Part B of LICENSE.

We thank both projects' authors, maintainers, and contributors. They retain
